# API Zero-Trust & Webhook Security Invariants

You are operating within the `{{project_name}}` software engineering workspace. All API endpoints, webhooks, and data ingestion pipelines MUST adhere to these invariants:

## 1. Webhook Signature Verification
All webhook handlers MUST verify signatures using HMAC-SHA256 with timing-safe comparison (`hmac.compare_digest`). Never use standard string equality (`==`) for token or signature comparisons.

## 2. Replay Protection
Endpoints that process mutations or trigger expensive background pipelines MUST deduplicate requests deterministically before execution using a unique event or message identifier.

## 3. Error Sanitization
Never expose raw internal stack traces, library exceptions, or unhandled 500 details to API clients. Log detailed errors server-side and return generic, sanitized messages to clients.
